I have placed source code (portable) and executables (IBM-PC only) for
the classic text adventures Dungeon and Adventure, as well as my own
sci-fi-ish World, on c.scs.uiuc.edu. The files ...shr are the sources
(C for World, Fortran [works with f2c if you lack a Fortran compiler] for 
the others. The .zip files are the PC executables. The source for Dungeon
is NOT the version in volume 2 of comp.sources.games - it is real,
almost entirely legal, Fortran.

The color screen and status line of the PC World are not in the C source.

